          "fact": "F5",
          "source": "lem-cdr-smooth-s4-complement-is-standard-ball",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Let B be a smooth 4-ball embedded in the standard smooth 4-sphere S⁴. The closure of S⁴\\B is diffeomorphic to the standard 4-ball. This is the special smooth Schoenflies complement assertion used after a capped contractible 4-manifold has been identified with standard S⁴; it does not assert the smooth 4-dimensional Poincaré conjecture.",
          "uses": [
            "2.3"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F6",
          "source": "lem-satellite-connected-sum-substitution",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Let P be a pattern and let K be a knot. Form a pattern P_K by tying K into a small arc of P in a ball disjoint from the solid-torus core, using the zero framing. For every knot J, the satellite P(K#J) is isotopic as an oriented knot to P_K(J). The pattern P_K has the same winding number as P.",
          "uses": [
            "3.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F7",
          "source": "lem-satellite-operator-preserves-concordance",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Let P⊂S¹×D² be a smooth oriented pattern. If oriented knots K₀ and K₁ are concordant in one of the four categories C_sm, C_top, C_ex or C^{1/n}, then P(K₀) and P(K₁) are concordant in the same category. Thus P induces a well-defined set map on each of these concordance sets.",
          "uses": [
            "1.1",
