          "quote": "Let $M$ be a compact connected Hausdorff manifold, $o\\in M$, and $R$ a unital ring. One can construct paths $\\gamma_x$ from $o$ to every $x\\in M$, with $\\gamma_o$ constant, by fixed rules from one finite atlas and finitely many connecting paths. Let $\\mathcal R$ be a right-$R$ local system with a supplied identification $\\mathcal R_o=R$ and transport given by left multiplication by units, with monodromy image $H\\le R^\\times$. Its twisted singular complex has an explicit chain decomposition $C_*(M;\\mathcal R)=C'_*\\oplus Q_*$ after a change of free bases, where $C'_0=R$, $C'_* $ is free, and $Q_*$ is contractible with its only nonzero differential an identity from degree one to degree zero. Moreover\n$$\\operatorname{im}(d'_1)=\\sum_{h\\in H}(h-1)R.$$\nThe decomposition and its dual cochain homotopy equivalences require no choice principle. In particular this image is principal if $H$ is cyclic, if it equals $R$, or if every right ideal of $R$ is principal.",
