          "id": "step-1-1",
          "claim": "For compact $K,L\\subset X$, write $C=C_*^{\\mathrm{sing}}(X;\\mathbb Z)$ and $A_K=C_*(X\\setminus K;\\mathbb Z)$, with analogous notation for $L$. Local cochains vanishing on $A_K$ are the relative local complex denoted $D_K$. Simplex by simplex, addition gives an onto map $D_K\\oplus D_L\\to D_{K\\cup L}$: a simplex not entirely outside $K\\cup L$ is not entirely outside at least one of $K,L$, so place its assigned coefficient in the first allowed summand. This is a degreewise lift, not asserted to commute with coboundaries. Its kernel consists of pairs $(a,-a)$ with $a$ vanishing on $A_K+A_L$. Thus there is a short exact cochain sequence with that kernel. The latter cochain complex computes the relative local cohomology supported in $K\\cap L$. Indeed $X\\setminus K$ and $X\\setminus L$ are open and cover $X\\setminus(K\\cap L)$; [F2] replaces their small-chain sum by the full complement. To see the relative comparison on cochains explicitly, extend its small-chain homotopy $D$ to all ambient simplex generators by zero on simplices not contained in this complement. Then $1-\\partial D-D\\partial$ maps complement chains to their small-chain sum and fixes the sum, while $D$ vanishes on the sum. The resulting quotient maps are inverse up to the displayed chain homotopy; transporting coefficients along the same affine paths gives the identical local-cochain comparison. Taking cohomology gives the supported exact sequence.",
