          "claim": "Restrict to pairs $K\\subset U$, $L\\subset V$ compact. These unions are cofinal among compact supports in $X$. For any compact $Q\\subset X$, choose finitely many relatively compact coordinate neighborhoods whose closures lie in one of $U,V$ and whose interiors cover $Q$. The union of the closures assigned to $U$, intersected with $Q$, is a compact $K\\subset U$; the analogous construction gives $L\\subset V$, with $Q=K\\cup L$. Only one finite cover is selected. The intersections $K\\cap L$ are cofinal for compact subsets of $U\\cap V$, since one may take $K=L$ equal to any such compact set. Excision in [F2] identifies the groups supported in $K$, $L$ and $K\\cap L$ with their groups in $U$, $V$ and $U\\cap V$. Take the filtered colimit of the exact sequences of step 1.1. It is exact directly: a representative in a colimit kernel vanishes at one common larger pair of supports, where exactness supplies its lift; a zero representative of a lift also becomes zero at a common larger pair. With [F1] this gives exactly the displayed compact-support sequence and its extension maps.",
