          "id": "step-3-1",
          "claim": "Compactness gives a finite $\\delta/4$-net of anchors $a_0=o,a_1,\\ldots,a_s$, with the basepoint added first. For each unordered distinct anchor pair of distance less than $\\delta$, put an edge in a finite graph and map it to the straight coordinate path in the least-index $B_j$ containing that pair; the reverse orientation uses the reversed path. Map each vertex to its anchor. For any $x\\in M$, let $a(x)$ be the least-index anchor at distance less than $\\delta/4$. Join $x$ to $a(x)$ by the straight path in the least-index $B_j$ containing them. These connectors have diameter less than $\\epsilon$ and are defined by finite lists and the chart formulas, without choosing a family of paths. At $o$ take the constant connector.",
