          "id": "step-4-1",
          "claim": "Let $\\ell$ be any based loop in $M$. Uniform continuity on its compact interval gives a finite subdivision such that each segment has image diameter less than $\\delta/4$. Write its successive endpoints as $x_i$ and anchors as $a_i=a(x_i)$. Then $d(a_i,a_{i+1})<3\\delta/4$, so the selected graph has an edge between successive distinct anchors; repeated anchors give the constant path. The loop formed by this edge, the original loop segment and the two endpoint connectors is contained in a set of diameter less than $4\\epsilon$: each connector and edge has diameter less than $\\epsilon$, and its initial or terminal point lies within $\\delta/4$ of an endpoint of the original short segment. This entire small loop therefore lies in one of the contractible coordinate balls of step 2.1. Contract it there. Gluing these finitely many homotopies, with adjacent connectors cancelling, shows that $\\ell$ is based homotopic to the resulting graph edge loop at $a_0=o$. Thus the fundamental-group map of the component of this finite graph containing $a_0$ is onto.",
