          "source": "lem-torsion-free-abelian-extensions-preserve-group-ring-domains",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Let $k$ be a commutative field and let $H\\trianglelefteq G$ be a normal subgroup with torsion-free abelian quotient $G/H$. If $k[H]$ has no zero divisors, then $k[G]$ has no zero divisors. The group extension need not split; neither finite generation of $G/H$ nor an order on all of $G$ is assumed.",
          "uses": [
