        },
        {
          "fact": "F2",
          "source": "lem-ptfa-groups-have-finite-folner-sets",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Every group admitting a finite subnormal series with torsion-free abelian factors satisfies the left Folner condition: for each finite subset $S$ and each $\\varepsilon>0$ there exists a finite nonempty subset $F$ with $|sF\\triangle F|<\\varepsilon|F|$ for every $s\\in S$. This assertion requires no countability or finite-generation hypothesis and no choice axiom. More generally the finite Folner condition is preserved by arbitrary group extensions whose kernel and quotient satisfy it.",
