          "source": "lem-folner-group-ring-domains-have-ore-fractions",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Let $k$ be a commutative field and let $G$ satisfy the finite left Folner condition. If $k[G]$ has no zero divisors, then it satisfies both Ore conditions: for nonzero $a,b\\in k[G]$ there exist nonzero $x,y$ with $ax=by$, and nonzero $u,v$ with $ua=vb$. Moreover it embeds as a unital subring in a division ring $D$ in which each element has the form $as^{-1}$ for $a\\in k[G]$ and $0\\ne s\\in k[G]$. Thus this is a skew field of fractions, rather than only a ring in which some denominators are invertible. The construction uses no choice axiom.",
          "uses": [
