          "claim": "Intrinsically send $\\bar v$ to the right-linear functional $w\\mapsto h(v,w)$. In a unitary frame this is $J:\\overline R\\to R$, $J(\\bar a)=\\bar a$, where the bar on the right is the ring involution. It is left-linear: $J(r\\cdot\\bar a)=\\overline{a\\bar r}=r\\bar a$. It commutes with transport, since $\\overline{ua}=\\bar a\\bar u=\\bar a u^{-1}$. Hence it identifies the conjugate chain-coefficient local system with the dual system of step 1.2. Conjugation changes neither underlying abelian-group cycles nor boundaries and is involutive, so the homology of that dual system identifies with $\\overline{H_*(C_*)}$. When $M$ is oriented and closed, apply [F2] to the actual dual local system from step 1.2, viewed as a local system of abelian groups with a commuting left-$R$ action. Its cap isomorphism gives precisely the displayed cohomology-to-conjugate-homology identification.",
