          "quote": "Let $M$ be a compact oriented boundaryless Hausdorff topological $n$-manifold and let $\\mathcal L$ be a local system of abelian groups. Cap with its integral orientation class induces isomorphisms\n$$H^p(M;\\mathcal L)\\xrightarrow{\\sim}H_{n-p}(M;\\mathcal L)$$\nfor every integer $p$, without a choice principle. The maps respect any coefficient-ring action commuting with transport, and in particular apply to local systems of modules over a noncommutative ring by forgetting to abelian groups and retaining that action. No smoothness, triangulation or prescribed finite CW structure is assumed.",
