          "quote": "Let $W$ be a compact oriented Hausdorff topological $n$-manifold with boundary $A$ and a supplied boundary collar $c:A\\times[0,1)\\to W$. Let $\\mathcal L$ be a local system of abelian groups. Cap with the integral relative orientation class $z=[W,A]$ gives isomorphisms in every integer degree:\n$$H^p(W,A;\\mathcal L)\\xrightarrow{\\sim}H_{n-p}(W;\\mathcal L),\\qquad H^p(W;\\mathcal L)\\xrightarrow{\\sim}H_{n-p}(W,A;\\mathcal L).$$\nThe maps commute with every coefficient action commuting with transport, including noncommutative ring actions on the underlying abelian-group systems. No choice principle, smoothness, triangulation or finite CW structure is assumed.",
