          "source": "def-poly-torsion-free-abelian-group",
          "source_section": "Definition",
          "quote": "A group G is poly-torsion-free abelian (PTFA) if it admits a finite subnormal series\n1=G_0 ◁ G_1 ◁ ⋯ ◁ G_m=G\nin which every quotient G_{j+1}/G_j is torsion-free abelian. The trivial group is PTFA, using the length-zero series. The term “subnormal” means each G_j is normal in G_{j+1}; normality in all of G is not required.",
