      "derivations": [
        {
          "id": "step-1-1",
          "claim": "Call the finite-free property for a group $L$ the implication that a right-$k[L]$ matrix map between finite free modules is injective if its augmentation is injective. If $L$ is torsion-free abelian, [F1] makes $k[L]$ a commutative ring without zero divisors. For an $n$ by $m$ matrix whose augmentation is injective, finite elimination over $k$ gives an $m$ by $m$ minor with nonzero augmented determinant. The determinant of that minor is therefore nonzero in $k[L]$. Multiplying a vector in its kernel by the adjugate shows that this nonzero determinant kills every coordinate. Absence of zero divisors forces all coordinates zero, so the original matrix is injective. This also covers the trivial group and empty matrices.",
