          "quote": "Let $\\mathcal L$ be one local system on $X$.\n\n1. If $Z\\subseteq A\\subseteq X$ and $\\overline Z\\subseteq\\operatorname{int}_X(A)$, inclusion induces excision isomorphisms in both local homology and local cohomology between $(X\\setminus Z,A\\setminus Z)$ and $(X,A)$, using the restrictions of $\\mathcal L$.\n2. For an open cover $X=U\\cup V$, there are natural exact sequences\n   $$\\cdots\\to H_n(U\\cap V;\\mathcal L)\\to H_n(U;\\mathcal L)\\oplus H_n(V;\\mathcal L)\\to H_n(X;\\mathcal L)\\to\\cdots$$\n   and\n   $$\\cdots\\to H^n(X;\\mathcal L)\\to H^n(U;\\mathcal L)\\oplus H^n(V;\\mathcal L)\\to H^n(U\\cap V;\\mathcal L)\\to\\cdots,$$\n   where all systems are restrictions and the middle difference map in cohomology is $u|_{U\\cap V}-v|_{U\\cap V}$.\n\nThe same conclusions hold for the standard excisive-cover condition after replacing the cover by interiors. A local system given only on a subspace is not silently assumed to extend to $X$.",
