          "quote": "Let $\\Gamma$ be PTFA and let $k$ be either $\\mathbb Z$ or a commutative field. The group ring $A=k[\\Gamma]$ has no zero divisors, satisfies both Ore conditions, and has a fraction division ring $K$ in which every element is both a right and a left fraction of elements of $A$. The involution $\\overline{\\sum c_g g}=\\sum c_g g^{-1}$ extends uniquely to an involutive anti-automorphism of $K$.\n\nEvery intermediate unital ring $A\\subseteq R\\subseteq K$ has no zero divisors, satisfies both Ore conditions, and has this same $K$ as its fraction division ring. If $R$ is stable under the extended involution, that involution restricts to $R$ and descends to its additive quotient $K/R$. None of these assertions requires a choice principle.",
